$E531 HitBoxes ; the box starts, one for each class of the other record
$E537 ; along: position - half (others 11-13)
$E53C ; - 2 more (others 4-10)
$E541 ; - 2 more, 4 in all (others 0-3)
$E548 ; across - half: written, not read by the scan
$E54D ; across - half - 2 (others 4-13)
$E552 ; across - half - 4 (others 0-3)
$E555 ; the box widths into the CP operands below
$E556 ; others 11-13: 2 x half + 1
$E55E ; others 4-10: + 4
$E566 ; others 0-3: + 8
$E56C ; every record, from $C000
$E56F c PairScan ; Hit test: the moving record against every record
> IX = the moving record, HL = the other. Records that are gone or dying are passed over. The other's class picks the box: its position along less the box start (BC) must be below the width, as must its position across less the start, and its height less IYL below 15. The width operands are self-modified by MoveRecord ($E555): the box is centred along for every class, and across for others of types 0-10; against types 11-13 the across box starts at $C2F4 and runs 2 lower than centred ($C2F3, the centred start, is written and not read). Pads (14) are never hit; dishes (15) only by the player, without a height test. A pair goes to the handler table at $EBAA, which skips the record itself (docs/07-objects.md 7.4, 7.6). The list's end goes to StoreMove.
$E570 ; the end of the list: done
$E576 ; gone
$E57A ; dying
$E586 PairByClass
$E594 ; 11-13
$E597 ; 14: pads are never hit
$E599 ; 15: dishes, only the player
$E5A2 ; along, a box 23 wide
$E5BA ; across, 23 wide; no height test
$E5C6 ; a hit: the handler table
$E5C9 PairWithBig ; the other is of types 0-3
$E5DC ; the width: self-modified, 2 x half + 9
$E5E1 ; across
$E5E8 ; self-modified like $E5DC
$E5EE ; the other's height
$E5F1 ; within 7 either way
$E5FB PairWithMid ; the other is of types 4-10
$E60E ; the width: self-modified, 2 x half + 5
$E61A ; self-modified like $E60E
$E62D PairWithSmall ; the other is of types 11-13
$E640 ; the width: self-modified, 2 x half + 1
$E645 ; across from $C2F4, not $C2F3
$E64C ; self-modified like $E640
$E57E c PairScanNext ; Drop the other record's address and go on
> Also the "nothing" handler of the hit table (docs/07-objects.md 7.6).
$E57F c PairScanStep ; The next record of the scan
> The pair scan moves on to the next record (HL + 16) and tests it against the moving record IX again (PairScan). Most pairs come by falling through PairScanNext (the other record gone or dying, or the "nothing" handler of the table); it is jumped to directly when the other record is the moving one itself and from HitShotOnTarget when an enemy shot passes a moving target; entered 640 205 times in the bot game (PairScan 656 852) (docs/04-game-loop.md 4.5, docs/07-objects.md 7.6).
$E65F c StoreMove ; Write the new position and height into the record
> From $C2F6 (height), $C2EA (along) and $C2F2 (across), into +4, +1/+2 and +3.
$E674 c NextMover ; The next live record to move
> Gone records (bit 7) are passed over; bit 6 ends the list.
$E687 b DownHeldCount ; Passes down has been held, up to 6: the aircraft's climb step
> $E687-$E68A: one counter for each stick direction, read by the player routine $E7E9; the step is (count + 1) / 2 (docs/10-gameplay-logic.md 10.3).
$E688 b UpHeldCount ; Passes up has been held, up to 6
$E689 b LeftHeldCount ; Passes left has been held, up to 6
$E68A b RightHeldCount ; Passes right has been held, up to 6
$E68B b AutoCountdown ; The AUTO countdown: passes left, 0 when off
> Set at the round start ($D251) and to $FF when the player reaches the barrier ($E4DE); counted down by $E68C (docs/05-controls.md 5.4).

# Range $E68C-$FFFF: input, player, sprites, hits, text, menu, sound, course blocks, IM 2 table

@module player
$E68C c ReadControls ; Input: the AUTO countdown, or the chosen device into the control byte
> Called once a pass by the play loop outside the demo (docs/04-game-loop.md 4.3, step 4). While the countdown $E68B runs it does not read the device: it prints " AUTO " ($64F6), or six spaces ($F136) on the pass that ends the count, requests sound bit 3, moves the convoy, steers the player 2 across toward $2C, sets the new height $C2F6 to the height - 1 (not below 2) plus (6 - count) / 2 over the last 6 passes, and sets the speed $C006 to 0 while the reserve $E7B8 lasts, else 1; the followers ($C066 + 16 * k) get the same speed. docs/05-controls.md 5.4, docs/10-gameplay-logic.md 10.4.
> With the countdown at 0 it reads the device chosen in the menu ($C28F: 0 keyboard, 1 Sinclair, 2 Kempston, 3 Protek-AGF) into the control byte $C290 (bit 0 left, 1 right, 2 down, 3 up, 4 fire, active high) and jumps to the player routine $E7E9. docs/05-controls.md 5.2-5.3.
$E68C ; AUTO countdown, set by the round setup ($D251) and at the barrier
$E696 ; the count reached 0: clear the message window
$E69B ; still counting: " AUTO " (the string stored in the font's spare slots)
$E69E PrintAutoText
$E6A1 ; the count, kept in A' for the height ease below
$E6A5 ; sound request bit 3: the AUTO beep
$E6AA ; the followers copy the leader
$E6AD ; position across: 2 a pass toward the middle of the track, $2C
$E6BA AutoAcrossUp
$E6BC AutoStoreAcross
$E6BF ; height - 1, but not below 2
$E6C7 AutoStoreHeight
$E6CB ; last 6 passes: + (6 - count) / 2
$E6DB AutoSpeed
$E6DD ; speed 0 while the reserve lasts, then 1
$E6E8 AutoStoreSpeed
$E6EC ; no followers: done
$E6F2 ; +6 (speed) of the four pod slots $C060-$C090
$E6FA AutoPodSpeedLoop
$E6FF ReadDevice ; $C28F: the device chosen in the menu
$E70E ReadKeyboard ; device 0: Q, A, K, L, fire on the bottom two rows
$E713 ; Q
$E71A ; bit 0 of $C000 (the vehicle type) decides whether Q is up or down
$E722 QIsDown
$E724 ReadKeyA ; A, the opposite of Q
$E733 AIsUp
$E735 ReadKeysKL ; L (bit 1) right, K (bit 2) left
$E73F ReadKeyK
$E744 ReadFireRows ; $7EFE selects the rows $7FFE and $FEFE together: any key there fires
$E74F StoreKeyboard
$E750 ; the control byte
$E756 ReadSinclair ; device 1, both Interface 2 rows: 1-5 left, right, down, up, fire as they are
$E75E ; 0, 9, 8, 7, 6 from bit 0: reversed below to line up with 1-5
$E767 ReverseBitsLoop ; five bits of C reversed into A
$E76C ; the two sticks ORed together
$E773 ReadKempston ; device 2: port $1F
$E776 ; down, up, fire as they are
$E778 ; Kempston right (bit 0) is the game's bit 1
$E77E KempstonLeft ; Kempston left (bit 1) is the game's bit 0
$E784 StoreKempston
$E789 ReadProtek ; device 3: the cursor keys 5, 6, 7, 8 and 0
$E78F ; 5: left
$E795 ProtekDown
$E799 ; 6: down
$E79F ProtekUp ; 7: up
$E7A5 ProtekRight ; 8: right
$E7AB ProtekFire ; 0: fire
$E7B1 StoreProtek
$E7B7 b FireCount ; Passes with fire held
> Counts the passes fire is held, 0 when released ($E7E9). A shot leaves on odd counts (every other pass), a shell of the ground vehicle only when bit 1 is clear as well (every fourth pass). docs/07-objects.md 7.7.
$E7B8 b SpeedReserve ; The ground vehicle's speed reserve
> Spent by slowing down (down held, or the AUTO start), earned back by speeding up (up held), at most 32; 10 at each round start. docs/10-gameplay-logic.md 10.3.
$E7B9 c ConvoyFollow ; The followers copy the one in front
> With followers ($ECE4 not 0) it walks the convoy links $ECE7-$ECF0 from the last to the first: each follower's position across (+3) takes the value of the record in front of it (the first follower takes the player's $C003), and while the player moves ($C006 not 0) the height (+4) too. Going from the back to the front makes each follower take its leader's value of the pass before: the convoy trails the player's moves. Called by $E68C (AUTO) and $E7E9. docs/07-objects.md 7.5, docs/10-gameplay-logic.md 10.4.
$E7B9 ; followers
$E7BE ; the last link: DE = its follower's +3
$E7C3 ConvoyLinkLoop
$E7CE ; BC = the link in front ($FF high byte: none)
$E7D6 ; across from the one in front
$E7D8 ; standing: the height is not copied
$E7E2 NextConvoyLink
$E7E9 c MovePlayer ; The player: shot life, firing
> Entered by a jump from the device readers. It moves the convoy, ages the player's five shots ($C010-$C050, +F counts passes; at 12 a shot not exploding is removed) and fires while bit 4 of $C290 is held: a shot every other pass into a free slot from template $C360, at the player's position + 4 along, its position across and 2 below its height; the ground vehicle (bit 0 of $C000) holding up as well lobs a shell instead, from template $C370 every fourth pass, its arc step +E set from the player's height against the arc table $C282. Sound request bit 4 per shot. Falls into $E8AF. docs/07-objects.md 7.7, docs/10-gameplay-logic.md 10.3.
